# F7: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material outside (a bore), opens upward; flat floor F9 -- a milled bore; rim at z=15.0, 5.0 below the stock top z=20.0 -- authored from its rim by z=, so the step above it is another feature's material (CHECKLIST row 2.3)
# finish the wall with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F7_Bore, stepover=...)  [stepover is the ring spacing up the wall]
# a flat floor is milled, not drilled -- a twist drill leaves a conical point, so no drill run is suggested
feature F7_Bore CylinderBore(dia=30.0, extent=10.0, x=35.0, y=40.0, z=15.0)

# F8: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material inside (a standing boss), flat top cap F10, clean base at z=15.0 (CHECKLIST row 2.4)
# finish the wall with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F8_Boss, stepover=...)  [stepover is the ring spacing up the wall]
# the tool rides outside at R + r_tool (convex flank; finish_cylinder's mirror)
feature F8_Boss CylinderBoss(dia=20.0, extent=5.0, x=70.0, y=40.0, z=15.0)

# F10: planar, normal +Z, topmost planar face (CHECKLIST row 1.1)
feature F10_Top Plane(z=20.0)
